    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:154`).\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n**Framework layer \u2014 before the method body runs:**\n\n1. **HTTP authentication** \u2014 Only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`: the request must be authenticated (HTTP Basic, `anyRequest().authenticated()`), else 401. When `=false`, `permitAll` skips this.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, via `@Valid @RequestBody` on the `@Validated` interface). Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**. Field constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (`^\\+?[0-9 ()\\-]+$`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `email` (optional) \u2014 `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional) \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`, `@Size(4..4)`\n3. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else `AccessDeniedException` \u2192 **403**. (Note: this fires *after* bean validation, so a malformed body yields 400 even for an unauthorized caller.)\n\n**Imperative validation inside the method (interleaved with normalization side-effects):**\n\n4. **Address** \u2014 normalized; blank after normalization \u2192 `InvalidAddressException` (400).\n5. **Telephone** \u2014 normalized to E.164 with national-length rules; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n6. **Disposable email domain** \u2014 rejects mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n7. **Postcode vs. city region** \u2014 out-of-range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400); skipped if postcode null or region unknown.\n8. **Future registration date** \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 `InvalidRegistrationDateException` (400).\n9. **Daily limit** \u2014 \u2265100 owners already registered for that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n10. **City capacity** \u2014 \u226550 owners in that city \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n11. **Household duplicate** \u2014 same household exists and `sharesHousehold` is false \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (**409**).\n12. **Identity in use** \u2014 `telephone|email|householdId` matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n1. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; `sharesHousehold` is read-only, not persisted).\n2. **Normalize fields** (mutating the entity): address (trim/collapse/uppercase/expand ST/RD/AVE), telephone (canonical E.164), email (lowercase), and **default registrationDate** to today if null then roll weekend dates forward to Monday.\n3. **Assign `householdId`** = hash(lastName, postcode) and **`householdSize`** = members + 1.\n4. **Set possible-duplicate flags** (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) \u2014 soft flag, never rejects; skipped for declared members or when postcode absent.\n5. **Assign derived fields**, in order: `namesakeCount` \u2192 `customerCode` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`) \u2192 `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 same-day signups).\n6. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 DB INSERT; identity-generated `id` populated.\n7. **Audit log line** to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n8. Build response DTO with computed display-only fields (displayName, initials, telephoneDisplay, membership points/level, locality, contact preference, Luhn check digit, age band).\n9. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`** header and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Worth noting\n\n- There are **no** `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate` callbacks, no custom `ConstraintValidator` on this path (the only one, `PetAgeValidator`, applies to pets), and **no** events, email, cache updates, or password encoding (owners have no password).\n- The uniqueness/capacity/household/identity checks (steps 9\u201312) are **application-level scans** \u2014 each re-queries *all* owners via `findAllOwners()` and filters in memory. There are no DB uniqueness constraints backing them, so they are **race-prone** under concurrent creates.\n- The entity also carries `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints (e.g. `Owner.telephone` requires `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`), but these normally never fire since values are already validated/normalized before save."
